## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/resample.html
- Summary (EN): The Resample node scales an image by changing its width, height and pixel size, producing a new output canvas that can have a different aspect ratio or resolution. An optional size reference sets the output size and metadata.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Resample redimensionne une image en changeant sa largeur, sa hauteur et la taille de ses pixels, sur un nouveau canevas de sortie.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the image to resample", "size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata; uses source when not wired"]

- Key parameters: ["Size Control: Resolution (pixel count), Aspect Ratio or Pixel Size", "Base Size: Parameter (values entered) or Size Input (inherited from size_ref or source)", "Base Resolution / Base Aspect Ratio / Pixel Size: base values when Base Size is Parameter", "Uniform Scale: scales the Base Size", "Resolution Scale: scales pixel count in width and height (Resolution mode)", "Fixed Dimension: keeps width, height, smaller or larger dimension fixed (Aspect Ratio mode)", "Size Scale: scales pixel width and height (Pixel Size mode)", "Reframe to Destination: stretches input to fill the output boundary so the display window matches the data window", "Filter: Point, Bilinear, Box, Bartlett, Catmull-Rom, Mitchell or B-spline", "Stretch Behavior: Stretch to Fit, Fit Horizontally, Fit Vertically, Fit Maximally or Fit Minimally"]

- Caveats: ["Stretch Behavior has no effect when Reframe to Destination is on", "Fixed Dimension applies only in Aspect Ratio mode; Size Scale only in Pixel Size mode", "The page does not state the default filter"]

